1. **Clause (d) of the safety rule is asserted, not measured.** `:328-331` claims "an error-in terminal is never a REQUIRED input". A subVI author may mark any connector-pane terminal *Required*. If `Clear Errors.vi`'s `error in (no error)` is Required in LV2026's vi.lib, v2 breaks the instant `w739` goes; B4 repairs it, but `[B3] after deleting #242` will read `0` and be blamed on the node delete.
