4. **Cold reopen.** The fact peer answered six minutes before this run (`archive/peer/2026-09-21-c64-execstate-recompile.md:74-90`): NI documents compilation as deferred to **load, run or save**; `ExecState` has four values and **no "needs recompile" state**; an independent ActiveX-scripting project hit persistent `eBad` after scripting until it **saved**. Stage C's cold reopen is then the first real compile verdict v2 ever gets — a `1` at `P_f` does not predict it, and a `0` does not prove brokenness. The same peer names `Compile.VI` (466) as the documented refresh; the run declares "NOTHING IN THIS FILE IS BUILT AGAINST IT" (`:197-198`).

